<title>BRAZIL: Paranagua port to strike from March 5 over pay.</title>
<headline>Paranagua port to strike from March 5 over pay.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Workers at the key Brazilian port of Paranagua will start a 24-hour strike from March 5 over pay and the strike will extend to all other Brazilian ports on March 6 if no agreement is reached, a union official said.</p>
<p>&quot;On Wednesday at 7 a.m. local (1000 GMT) we will begin a strike of 24 hours,&quot; said Nelson Bandeira, secretary of the Paranagua Unions Council.</p>
<p>&quot;On Thursday at 7 a.m. local, the strike will take effect on a national level and will last 48 hours,&quot; he said.</p>
</text>
